  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat is the weekly food cost for Kory's dog? Kory's dog weighs 64 pounds. Dog food for Elijah's and Kory's dogs costs 2 dollars per pound.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 6; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"Good, now using that, can you calculate: What is the combined weight of Elijah's two dogs and Kory's dog in pounds? One more thing you should know: Elijah has another dog that weighs half as much as Kory's dog.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"Kory’s dog weighs \\\\(60\\\\) pounds.\\n\\n- Elijah’s first dog weighs one-third as much:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\times 60=20\\\\text{ pounds}\\n\\\\]\\n\\n- Elijah’s second dog weighs half as much:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\times 60=30\\...\n- {\"content\":\"One more thing — Kory's dog eats 3 pounds of dog food each week.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"Kory’s dog eats \\\\(3\\\\) pounds of food per week at \\\\(\\\\$2\\\\) per pound:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n3 \\\\times 2 = 6\\n\\\\]\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\\\$6\\\\text{ per week}}\\n\\\\]\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Elijah has one dog that weighs one-fourth as much as Kory's dog.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Elijah’s dog’s weight does not affect Kory’s dog’s food cost. Kory’s dog eats \\(3\\) pounds of food per week, at \\(\\$2\\) per pound:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 2 = 6\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$6\\text{ per week}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
