  "task_assistant_messages": [
    "The weekly food cost cannot be determined from the information given. We need to know how many pounds of food Kory’s dog eats each week.\n\nIf the dog eats \\(F\\) pounds per week, then:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Cost}=2F\n\\]\n\nSo the answer is \\(\\boxed{\\$2F}\\), with the weekly food amount \\(F\\) still unspecified.",
    "Elijah’s two dogs eat **5 pounds** of dog food each week altogether.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{5\\text{ pounds}}\n\\]",
    "Kory’s dog weighs **60 pounds**, but the weekly amount of food it eats is still not specified. Therefore, its weekly food cost cannot be determined.\n\nIf it eats \\(F\\) pounds of food per week:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Weekly cost} = \\$2F}\n\\]",
    "Kory’s dog weighs \\(60\\) pounds. Elijah’s dog weighs one-third as much:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{3}\\times 60=20\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Elijah’s dog weighs:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{20\\text{ pounds}}\n\\]",
